  "name": "pharmacy-counselling-script",
  "description": "Write the counselling a patient will actually follow when collecting a new or changed medicine — what it is for, how to take it, what to expect, and the one thing that would make them stop. Use when asked to write patient counselling, counsel on a new prescription, explain a medicine to a patient, or improve adherence at the counter. Produces the counselling script in plain language, the teach-back questions, the red-flag advice, the adherence anticipation, and the documentation line. A communication framework for a licensed pharmacist; it makes no clinical determination and substitutes for no product-specific information.",
